Related Work
\subsection{Self-Driving Vehicle}
Self-driving vehicles have been widely studied in recent years. The general system framework of SVs can be divided into three parts: perception, decision-making, and control. The perception module can be divided into three parts: localization, mapping, and detection. Localization is to obtain the position of the vehicle in the map. Mapping is to obtain the map information around the vehicle. Detection is to detect obstacles around the vehicle. The decision-making module is to decide the driving behavior of the vehicle. The control module is to control the vehicle to execute the driving behavior. In the decision-making module, there are two main types of methods, rule-based methods and learning-based methods. Rule-based methods include behavior tree, decision tree, fuzzy logic, and expert system, etc. Learning-based methods include reinforcement learning, imitation learning, and deep learning, etc. The decision-making module can be further divided into three parts: planning, prediction, and decision. Planning is to plan the path and trajectory of the vehicle. Prediction is to predict the future movement of obstacles. Decision is to decide the driving behavior of the vehicle.

