\centering
\includegraphics[width=1\textwidth]{Figure/flow_chart.png}
\caption{The overview of our proposed method.}
\label{fig:flow_chart}
\end{figure*}

In this paper, we propose a novel deep learning-based method for image deblurring. Our method utilizes a CNN to learn the mapping from the blurry image to the sharp image. The CNN-based method has shown promising results in various deblurring tasks, including deblurring of the entire image, deblurring of the human face, and deblurring of the human body. The proposed method is designed to handle the blur caused by various sources, such as object motion, camera shake, and scene depth variation. We also present a new large-scale dataset that provides pairs of realistic blurry images and their corresponding ground truth sharp images. The proposed model trained on this dataset achieved state-of-the-art performance in dynamic scene deblurring. The main contributions of this paper are as follows:
\begin{itemize}
\item We propose a novel deep learning-based method for image deblurring that utilizes a CNN to learn the mapping from the blurry image to the sharp image.
\item We present a new large-scale dataset that provides pairs of realistic blurry images and their corresponding ground truth sharp images.
\item We evaluate the proposed method on various deblurring tasks and achieve state-of-the-art performance in dynamic scene deblurring.
\end{itemize}

