 With the increasing popularity and decreasing cost of video capture devices, there has been a phenomenal surge in videos captured everyday. Facing with the sheer amount of video data, it is becoming more and more difficult for a user to browse all these videos completely to seek useful information. As a result, it has been very demanding to develop some intelligent  systems that can automatically generate summaries of videos for human viewers. In recent years, the problem of video summarization has attracted increasing attention from the multimedia and computer vision community \cite{arxivID-2210.11707-0}. A lot of research efforts have been made on this topic, and the main focus is to generate a minimum subset of frames or shots which can still convey the main story of the original video.

\begin{figure}[t]
\centering
\includegraphics[width=8cm]{figure1.pdf}
\caption{An example of video summarization. The proposed unsupervised method is able to automatically generate a video summary from the original video.}
\label{fig:example}
